Z||000010||Steven||06-11-2001||02:37 PM||||Come to think of it you did say the you where using the TDC pistons in post <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/007777.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/007777.html</A>  But the pistons in that block look like dish pistons. I see that their is a number on the top of the piston, could you please get a picture of them so we could see the part numbers. Also I see the timing chain is on, did you degree the cam yet? Keep us posted! <P>------------------<BR> 85 Fiero GT<BR> 3.2 Liter Under Construction||||reg||1
Z||000011||88formula||06-11-2001||04:47 PM||||See the holes in that piston.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Holes_in_piston.JPG"> <BR>The hack machinist that balanced my reciprocating assembly drilled holes in the original pistons to lighten them. I was so f$%^&ing pissed when I saw this. He screwed up most all the machine work that was done This is why it has taken me this long to get the engine back together. I had to bring all the parts to another more reputable and expensive machine shop and have everything corrected.<P>Here is a picture of the H684CP pistons I originally had.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Top_of_DOHC_piston.JPG"> <BR>Here is a picture of the H800P Hypereutectic pistons I have now. These are replacement pistons for the 95 ohv 3.4-liter engine except they are hypereutectic pistons.  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Top_of_piston.JPG">  <BR>My compression ratio will be 9.06 with these pistons on average. <P><BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
